<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    C4, "Hierarchy": one circled cell and the four eliminations it forces.

    The geometry, because every number in here was chosen against a constraint
    rather than by eye:

      canvas      108 x 108, the adaptive-icon standard
      visible     the middle 72 (18..90) is all the launcher guarantees
      safe        a circle of radius 33 from centre (54,54) — no mask clips it
      cell pitch  36, so the grid rules fall at 36 and 72 and the circled cell
                  is the middle one
      ring        r 15.5, stroke 7, centred — comfortably inside the safe circle
      crosses     centred 36 out, arms 6 long, stroke 4.4, alpha 0.82

    The crosses are deliberately lighter and thinner than the ring. Two reasons.
    The hierarchy is the meaning — the ring is the mark, the crosses are what it
    did — and shorter arms reach 42 units from centre instead of 44, so a
    circular mask grazes a tip rather than taking a limb. Full-weight crosses at
    this pitch cannot be made safe without shrinking the ring to r 10, which
    gives back most of what made this design worth choosing.

    The grid rules run off all four edges on purpose: the chart continues past
    the frame, and it means the icon fills its tile under a square mask instead
    of floating in a ring of empty ground.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The implied grid. Faint, and off the edges. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M36,6V102 M72,6V102 M6,36H102 M6,72H102"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeAlpha="0.28"
        android:strokeWidth="3"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />

    <!-- The four forced eliminations: up, down, left, right of the circle. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M12,48l12,12 M24,48l-12,12 M84,48l12,12 M96,48l-12,12 M48,12l12,12 M60,12l-12,12 M48,84l12,12 M60,84l-12,12"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeAlpha="0.82"
        android:strokeWidth="4.4"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />

    <!-- The circled cell. Two half-arcs, because path data has no circle. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M38.5,54a15.5,15.5 0 1,0 31,0a15.5,15.5 0 1,0 -31,0"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="7" />

</vector>
